### R1. Disagreements & Accepted Corrections

**Overstated or imprecise claims in Consultant C ([grhremark_1.codex.out](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/grhremark_1.codex.out)):**
- **Guinand–Weil variance positivity for $4/11$ ([grhremark_1.codex.out:23, 30](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/grhremark_1.codex.out#L23)):** Wrong inequality direction and wrong term. Spectral variance positivity gives a *lower* bound ($\ge 0$), whereas `Prop DC` requires an *upper* bound $\phi_2 \le \eta_2/4$ ([pc3_results.md:138-140](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/pc3_results.md#L138-L140)). Moreover, non-principal character errors at $u \asymp D^{4/11}$ already decay as $e^{-cD^\theta\lambda^2} \ll D^{-A}$ unconditionally ([pc3_results.md:215, 224](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/pc3_results.md#L215-L224); [mf2L_results.md:48-55](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/mf2L_results.md#L48-L55)); the $D^{-2\alpha}$ wall is purely *principal-character* ([thmAB_results.md:379-413](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/thmAB_results.md#L379-L413)).
- **Genus-2 `Theorem R` constant $c = 2$ under RH alone ([grhremark_1.codex.out:5](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/grhremark_1.codex.out#L5)):** Overstated as unconditional given RH. In [genus2rh_results.md:9-23, 560-567](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/genus2rh_results.md#L9-L23), $c = 2$ still relies on Younis's *unrefereed v1 preprint* (`arXiv:2409.05761v1`) or an unverified referee sketch; from checked inputs RH gives $c = 3/\sqrt{2}$. C also omits SNFS `(O2)` ([snfsrig_results.md:60-67](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/snfsrig_results.md#L60-L67)).
- **Primitive-only Dirichlet GRH Lean check ([grhremark_1.codex.out:36](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/grhremark_1.codex.out#L36)):** Composite-modulus reductions (`detGRH`, `zroute`) invoke imprimitive characters $\bmod\, N$ ([detGRH_results.md:138-145](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/detGRH_results.md#L138-L145)); checking primitive $\chi$ suffices in Lean only if the imprimitive Euler-factor bridge on $0 < \operatorname{Re} s < 1$ is also verified.
- **Inventory omissions ([grhremark_1.codex.out:6-8, 22](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/grhremark_1.codex.out#L6-L8)):** Misses `Prop IWD` (IW hardness alone $\Rightarrow$ deterministic $L[1/2]$ under Dirichlet GRH, [dsr_results.md:304-310](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/dsr_results.md#L304-L310)), unconditional model barriers (`selfred Theorem L`, [selfred_results.md:380-388](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/selfred_results.md#L380-L388); tightened `cuspcoef Theorem DFB`, [cuspcoef_results.md:196](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/cuspcoef_results.md#L196)), and `almostall13` $C_\chi\delta$ removal.

**Corrections from Consultant C & Orchestrator accepted into G's answer:**
- **Dedekind $\Rightarrow$ Dirichlet hierarchy & $\infty$-types ([grhremark_1.codex.out:8](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/grhremark_1.codex.out#L8)):** All-field Dedekind GRH ($\zeta_{\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_N)}$) implies Dirichlet GRH (which G's Q1 treated as disjoint), whereas dBPW's full Arakelov walk ([nested_results.md:159-160](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nested_results.md#L159-L160)) needs Hecke characters with nontrivial $\infty$-types beyond $\zeta_K$.
- **Splitting-field GRH (`detGRH` row 9, [grhremark_1.codex.out:7](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/grhremark_1.codex.out#L7)):** Discharges deterministic fixed-degree Hensel prime selection ([detGRH_results.md:392](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/detGRH_results.md#L392)), omitted in G's Q1(b).
- **Overclaiming GRH relevance in G's Thread 3 ([grhremark_1.agy2.out:38-41](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/grhremark_1.agy2.out#L38-L41)):** Fully accepted — see R2(a).
- **Effort/confidence calibration ([grhremark_1.codex.out:29](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/grhremark_1.codex.out#L29)):** C's 60% (2–4 weeks) for end-to-end referee-ready $3/8$ consolidation is better calibrated than G's 80% ([mf2L_results.md:79-80](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/mf2L_results.md#L79-L80)).

---

### R2. Adjudication of the Three Proposals

- **(a) Pooled Lee–Venkatesan fields + `XK-Z` + `Prop PIN` for Las Vegas $L[1/3]$:**
  - **Verdict:** **Orchestrator is right; demote.** In `detGRH Prop Z` ([detGRH_results.md:324-329](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/detGRH_results.md#L324-L329)), once $\lambda(N) \mid D$, $H = \{a \in U : a^{2^k t} \in \{\pm 1\}\}$ has index $\ge 2$, so *random* Miller bases split $N$ w.p. $\ge 1/2$ **without GRH**. Dirichlet GRH only ensures $\langle -1, Q_0 \rangle = (\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$ (or $\langle -1, \mathrm{FB}\rangle = (\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$, which Burgess alone does not give at $B = L_N[1/3]$, [detGRH_results.md:145, 254](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/detGRH_results.md#L254)). The real bottleneck is `zroute` §3.2 seedless `PIN` ([zroute_results.md:223, 308-316](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md#L308-L316)): avoiding rational hyperplanes $w \in (\mathbb{Q}^n)^*$ on conditioned smooth exponent vectors $e(a - bm_j)$ after unit elimination (`detGRH` `(Z3)`, [detGRH_results.md:358-364](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/detGRH_results.md#L358-L364)) — the $\mathbb{Q}$-span twin of `Conjecture F` ([nfsfruit_results.md:32-40](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nfsfruit_results.md#L32-L40)). `remark.pdf` gives zero help on it.
  - **Corrected probability:** **3–5%**.
  - **Precise missing lemma (`Hyp PIN-LV`):** For $J = L_N[1/3, c']$ i.i.d. LV fields $(m_j, f_j)$ ([nfsfruit_results.md:83-91](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/nfsfruit_results.md#L83-L91)) with `XK-Z` torsion spaces $W_j \subseteq \mathbb{Q}^{\mathrm{FB}}$, $\Pr[Q_0 \subseteq \sum_{j=1}^J W_j + \mathbb{Q}e_{-1}] \ge 1/2$ (cancelling all $\mathrm{FB}\setminus Q_0$ coordinates over $\mathbb{Q}$, [zroute_results.md:223](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/zroute_results.md#L223)).

- **(b) Bost / Arakelov slope inequality for `grdeg` door (i) (barrier direction):**
  - **Verdict:** **Plausible for `G-height` (after fixing $\max_j \to$ tuple height), NOT implied by `Prop RR`, and leaves `G-count` heuristic.** `Prop RR` ([grdeg_results.md:133-151, 264-268](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/grdeg_results.md#L133-L151)) is a 2-generator resultant charging *one* linking congruence ($\kappa_{\text{gen}} \sim e/d \implies L[1/4]$ when $m = r/e \asymp x^{1/4} \ll n = d/e \asymp x^{1/2}$). Relativizing `rank3 Prop R4` ([rank3_results.md:72-75](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/rank3_results.md#L72-L75)) over $\mathcal{O}_k$ via Bost's slope inequality charges all $m-1$ congruences mod $\ker(\psi : \mathcal{O}_k \twoheadrightarrow \mathbb{Z}/N)$ while filtering degenerate subbundles, **but** G's $\max_j h_k(w_j)$ was misstated (generators can peak at disjoint places); it bounds the *projective tuple height*, matching `RR3`'s model status without solving box-counting (`V_F = \infty`, `H5_r` failure, [grdeg_results.md:95-99](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/grdeg_results.md#L95-L99)).
  - **Corrected probability:** **~35%** for the `G-height` lemma ($<1\%$ for a sub-$1/3$ algorithm).
  - **Precise missing lemma (`Relative R4`):** For any $m$ $\mathcal{O}_k$-independent elements $u^{(1)}, \dots, u^{(m)}$ of a rank-$m$ linked $\mathcal{O}_k$-submodule of $\mathcal{O}_K \times \mathcal{O}_{K'}$ ($[K:k]=n$, not confined to a lower-rank sublattice), $\sum_{v \mid \infty} \max_{1 \le k \le m} \log |u^{(k)}|_v \ge \frac{m-1}{2n-1}\log N - O(dn)$.

- **(c) Variance positivity for the $4/11$ three-level target:**
  - **Verdict:** **G is right; `remark.pdf`'s method does not touch principal-character drift.** At $\alpha = 4/11$ ($i=2$), $\eta_2 \asymp D^{-8/11}$, while `LF-A`/`OPV-A` ([thmAB_results.md:379-413](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/thmAB_results.md#L379-L413); [pc3_results.md:229-242, 348-354](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/pc3_results.md#L348-L354)) give gcd-factor and $\beta$-drift variance $\asymp \gamma^2\lambda^2 \asymp D^{-8/11}\lambda^C$ from the pole/saddle $s = \beta$, completely independent of zeros or explicit-formula positivity ([multidescent_results.md:70-72](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/multidescent_results.md#L70-L72)). Progress on $4/11$ can only come from classical `Prop DC_e` profile conditioning.
  - **Corrected probability:** **`< 1%`** via `remark.pdf`; **10–15%** via classical `DC_e` conditioning.
  - **Precise missing lemma:** Environment cells $e(A)$ (gcd + archimedean profiles, not pinning $A$) under which $\mathbb{E}_w[\phi_{2,e}], \mathbb{E}_w[\sigma_{2,e}^2] \le \eta_2/4$ at $\alpha = 4/11$ ([pc3_results.md:142-154, 348-354](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/pc3_results.md#L142-L154)).

---

### R3. Joint Verdict & Merged Top-3 Threads

**Joint verdict:** No — both consultants agree there is no credible path below $L_N[1/3]$ ($P < 1\text{–}2\%$), whether from RH/GRH/ERH as theorems or from the theta-lift and positivity methods sketched in `remark.pdf`. Every sub-$L[1/3]$ bottleneck in the repository is Diophantine or information-theoretic (resultant/size–entropy floors and candidate-construction costs, [completeness_audit_results.md:62-69](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/completeness_audit_results.md#L62-L69)), which $L$-function zero locations leave untouched. The lone open sub-$L[1/3]$ model crack (`grdeg` door (i)) has no candidate construction and is expected to close back to $\alpha \ge 1/3$.

**Merged top-3 next threads:**
1. **Consolidate unconditional rigorous $L_N[3/8]$** — prove `Hyp U′` under `DW` and merge `2L-MF` + `Lemma SPR-P′` ([audit2L_audit.md:76-78](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/audit2L_audit.md#L76-L78); [mf2L_results.md:56-60](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/mf2L_results.md#L56-L60)). **Probability:** 65–70%. **Cost:** Low–Medium (2–4 weeks; independent of `remark.pdf`).
2. **Close `grdeg` door (i) (`G-height`) via Bost slope / `Relative R4` over $\mathcal{O}_k$** (paired with searching for a counterexample witness, [grdeg_results.md:66-80, 264-268](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/grdeg_results.md#L66-L80)). **Probability:** ~35% for the barrier ($<1\%$ for a sub-$1/3$ algorithm). **Cost:** Low–Medium (1–2 weeks).
3. **Test borderline rigorous $L_N[4/11]$ via classical `Prop DC_e` gcd/archimedean conditioning** (dropping `remark.pdf`'s variance trick, [pc3_results.md:142-157, 348-354](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/pc3_results.md#L348-L354)). **Probability:** 10–15%. **Cost:** Medium (4–8 weeks). *(Pooled-LV `PIN-LV` drops to #4 at 3–5%.)*
